1. How do you handle secrets in Kubernetes securely?

Answer:
 • Use Kubernetes Secrets (base64 encoded, not encrypted by default).
 • Enable Encryption at Rest for secrets in etcd.
 • Integrate with external secret stores like HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault using external secret controllers.
 • Restrict access with RBAC.

