6. How do you scale Kubernetes clusters automatically?

Answer:
 • Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA): scales pods based on CPU/memory/metrics
 • Vertical Pod Autoscaler (VPA): adjusts resource requests/limits
 • Cluster Autoscaler: adds/removes nodes based on pending pods
 • Integrate with cloud providers (AWS, GCP, Azure) for dynamic node scaling

