8. How do you ensure zero downtime during Kubernetes upgrades?

Answer:
 • Upgrade control plane and worker nodes gradually
 • Use PodDisruptionBudgets (PDBs) to control eviction
 • Ensure Deployments use RollingUpdate strategy
 • Use readiness probes so traffic only routes to healthy pods
 • If using managed services (EKS/AKS/GKE), rely on cluster upgrade workflows

9. How do you enforce security policies cluster-wide?

Answer:
 • Use RBAC for access control
 • Use Pod Security Admission (PSA) to enforce pod-level restrictions
 • Use OPA Gatekeeper or Kyverno for custom policy enforcement
 • Scan container images with tools like Trivy, Aqua, or Clair
 • Enable audit logging on API server
